# Abstract
abstract: >
  This repository contains the complete Python code for probabilistic 
  cost risk assessment of the Adana City Hospital PPP project in Turkey 
  using the Chang & Ko (2017) lognormal modeling methodology. 
  
  The code performs correlated Monte Carlo simulation with 10,000 iterations, 
  computing Value at Risk (VaR), Conditional VaR (CVaR), probability of 
  cost overrun, sensitivity analysis, and scenario analysis. 
  
  The implementation is designed for reproducibility and transparency in 
  healthcare infrastructure risk research. The notebook is compatible 
  with Google Colab and local Jupyter environments.

